{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"22 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,31.75,3.651,3.268,"LG Electronics India"],[13.889,14.731,28.145,2.373,2.124,"Back to FY25 earnings, at 52x"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"LG Electronics India has slipped 3% since its Q2 FY27 results on 5 November"],[13.889,22.289,52.934,1.809,1.634,"while the NIFTY rose 5%, yet at ₹1,732 it still trades at 52x FY27 consensus"],[13.889,23.733,52.966,1.809,1.634,"EPS. That consensus, ₹33.23, is only 2% above the ₹32.46 earned in FY25:"],[13.889,25.177,52.966,1.809,1.634,"profit fell 24% in FY26 as a weaker rupee, dearer commodities and channel"],[13.889,26.621,52.966,1.809,1.634,"spending cut the EBITDA margin to 9.8% from 12.8%. Q2 itself was good:"],[13.889,28.065,52.987,1.809,1.634,"revenue grew 20% to ₹7,380 cr and net profit 26% to ₹489 cr. But cash from"],[13.889,29.509,52.931,1.809,1.634,"operations was ₹164 cr negative in the quarter as dealers were stocked for the"],[13.889,30.954,39.379,1.809,1.634,"festive season, and ₹870 cr went into the new Sri City plant."],[13.889,33.439,52.934,1.809,1.634,"1) In H2 FY27E revenue grows 15%, in line with consensus and mid-teens"],[13.889,34.883,52.936,1.809,1.634,"guidance, and net profit 24%, close to H1’s 26.5%. Consensus needs H2 profit"],[13.889,36.328,52.964,1.809,1.634,"up 42%. Our FY27E EPS of ₹31.07 is 7% below it, on an EBITDA margin of"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"10.6%, inside the “early double-digit” guide. 2) Sri City starts compressors in"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Q3 FY27 and air conditioners in Q4, doubling capacity; appliance EBIT margin"],[13.889,40.684,52.934,1.809,1.634,"rises to 10.8% in FY28E and EPS grows 17%. 3) The ₹5,000 cr plant absorbs"],[13.889,42.128,52.094,1.809,1.634,"the cash: free cash flow is negative in FY27E and net cash stays near ₹4,470 cr."],[13.889,44.59,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹1,110 averages two methods. The peer-median forward"],[13.889,46.034,52.934,1.809,1.634,"P/E of 38x (Voltas, Blue Star, Havells, Whirlpool, Crompton), on earnings"],[13.889,47.502,52.951,1.809,1.634,"twelve months ahead, gives ₹1,577. A ten-year DCF at a 12% cost of equity,"],[13.889,48.946,52.931,1.809,1.634,"plus net cash, gives ₹634 (₹740 at 11%). The legs are far apart; at ₹1,732 the"],[13.889,50.39,52.936,1.809,1.634,"shares need free cash flow to grow 31% a year to FY37E, against our 12%;"],[13.889,51.834,52.931,1.809,1.634,"consensus targets ₹1,955. What would prove us wrong: margins back above"],[13.889,53.278,52.936,1.809,1.634,"FY25’s as compressors are made in-house, or exports scaling faster. Risks: a hot"],[13.889,54.722,52.931,1.809,1.634,"summer in Q4, when LG sells about 55% of its air conditioners; a DRI notice"],[13.889,56.167,35.182,1.809,1.634,"seeking ₹154 cr of customs duty on royalty payments."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,67.265,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,200"],[14.451,64.904,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,400"],[14.451,62.554,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,600"],[14.451,60.195,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,800"],[17.913,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.539,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.326,67.96,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.08,67.96,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.3,69.131,3.918,1.275,1.111,"LG India ("],[22.222,69.157,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.835,69.131,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.919,69.131,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.266,70.291,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[26.459,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[31.202,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,70.291,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,71.356,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.346,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"13.8%"],[25.54,71.356,2.26,1.387,1.209,"1.5%"],[30.283,71.356,2.26,1.387,1.209,"6.0%"],[34.079,71.356,2.26,1.387,1.209,"2.8%"],[15.492,72.421,1.476,1.387,1.209,"Rel"],[19.34